{
  "borough": "London Borough of Barking and Dagenham",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development, by virtue of its massing and siting, would represent an&nbsp;inappropriate backland development&nbsp;that disrupts the established pattern of dwellings with direct street frontages and spacious rear gardens, which provide valuable spatial breaks and contribute to the area&#39;s character.&nbsp;The single-storey nature of the bungalow and its lack of a defined street presence would fail to integrate with the prevailing built form, appearing as an ancillary outbuilding rather than a standalone dwelling. As such, the proposal would appear incongruous and discordant, causing harm to the visual amenity, openness, and spatial character of the area, contrary to:Paragraphs 131 and 135 of the National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (December 2024)Policy D4 of the London Plan (March 2021)Policies SP2, DMD1 and DMD4 of the LBBD Local Plan (September 2024)",
    "The proposed development,&nbsp;on account of its massing and siting&nbsp;within a rear garden setting, the proposed development is at odds with the surrounding pattern of development and would&nbsp;in harm to neighbouring occupiers particularly nos. 24 Alexandra Road, resulting in a loss of outlook and causing an overbearing impact.&nbsp;The additional generation of noise, comings and goings and general disturbances will also result in harm, especially noting the vehicular noise generated from the associated, out of place&nbsp;car-parking space. The development would therefore constitute&nbsp;unneighbourly&nbsp;development and is contrary to:Policies D6 and D14 of the London Plan (March 2021)Policies DMD1 and&nbsp;DMSI 3 of the LBBD Local Plan&nbsp;&nbsp;(September 2024)"
  ],
